program switch_const_cases

? Bare int constants are valid `on` values: they fold to literals in C case
? labels (constants emit as variables/getters, which C rejects there).

TINT_RED: 1
TINT_GREEN: 2

@ color_name |c:int| string:
	switch c:
		on TINT_RED: return "red"
		on TINT_GREEN: return "green"
		_: return "other"
	$
$

@ main ||:
	expected: []

	a: color_name|1|
	print|a|
	expected.push|"red"|

	b: color_name|2|
	print|b|
	expected.push|"green"|

	c: color_name|9|
	print|c|
	expected.push|"other"|

	print|expected|
$
